# Modals & Row Interactions

Three mutually exclusive ways to react to a row click: open a modal, run a callback, or follow a link. Pick at most one — the table picks the first one that's defined and ignores the others.

## Open a modal

A Svelte component that receives [`ModalProps<Data>`](/api-reference/index/interfaces/ModalProps). The library handles open/close state; the component focuses on rendering the row details.

```typescript
import UserDataModal from './UserDataModal.svelte';

const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    // ...
    modalComponent: UserDataModal,
    autoOpenSingleItem: false,
    highlightedItemId: '42'
};
```

The modal component (daisyUI flavour):

```svelte
<script lang='ts'>
    import type { ModalProps } from 'svelte-advanced-datatable';
    import type { UserData } from './UserData.js';

    let { item }: ModalProps<UserData> = $props();
</script>

<div class='py-4 flex flex-wrap gap-6'>
    <img
        class='w-32 h-32 rounded-full ring ring-base-300'
        src='https://ui-avatars.com/api/?format=svg&name={item.firstName}+{item.lastName}'
        alt='{item.firstName} {item.lastName}'
    />
    <div class='flex-1'>
        <h4 class='text-lg font-semibold'>
            {item.firstName} {item.lastName}
            <small class='text-base-content/60'>@{item.userName}</small>
        </h4>
        <p class='mt-2'>
            Contact: <a class='link' href='mailto:{item.mailAddress}'>{item.mailAddress}</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
```

## Run a callback

```typescript
const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    // ...
    onItemClick: (item) => track('user.row.clicked', item.id)
};
```

Use when row clicks should drive app state without a built-in modal — open a side panel, kick off an inline edit, route to a side-effect.

## Navigate to a URL

```typescript
const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    // ...
    buildItemUrl: (item) => `/users/${item.id}`
};
```

The row renders as an `<a>` — middle-click and keyboard navigation behave correctly. Don't combine with `modalComponent` or `onItemClick`.

## Options

| Option                | Type                              | Description                                                                                                | Default     |
|:----------------------|:----------------------------------|:-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:------------|
| `modalComponent`      | `Component<ModalProps<Data>>`     | Svelte component rendered when a row is clicked.                                                            | —           |
| `onItemClick`         | `(item: Data) => void`            | Callback fired when a row is clicked. Mutually exclusive with `buildItemUrl`.                              | —           |
| `buildItemUrl`        | `(item: Data) => string`          | Turn each row into a link by returning the URL. Mutually exclusive with `onItemClick`.                     | —           |
| `autoOpenSingleItem`  | `boolean`                         | When the result has exactly one row, open the modal automatically. Only honoured with `modalComponent`.    | `false`     |
| `highlightedItemId`   | `string`                          | ID of the row that should receive the `highlighted` CSS class.                                              | —           |

## Click bubbling from custom cells

Custom cells with their own click handlers must call `event.stopPropagation()` — otherwise the row's click handler fires too, opening the modal or navigating away. See [Columns → Custom cell patterns](/docs/guides/columns#componenttypecustom).

<ExampleTable path='daisy-ui/modal' description='modalComponent receiving the clicked row; localised through svelte-i18n.' />

